//democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk/documents/s235747/2-treasury-management-outturn-2025-26-final.pdf","committee":"Investment Committee","date":"20/07/2026","key":false},{"title":"1. Treasury Management Update as at 31 May 2026_FINAL","url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk/documents/s235744/1-treasury-management-update-as-at-31-may-2026-final.pdf","committee":"Investment Committee","date":"20/07/2026","key":false},{"title":"1.3 Treasury Management Update as at 31 May 2026_Appendix 3_FINAL","url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk/documents/s235746/1-3-treasury-management-update-as-at-31-may-2026-appendix-3.pdf","committee":"Investment Committee","date":"20/07/2026","key":false}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Pensions Committee","time":"1.45 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Policy and Resources Committee","time":"1.45 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-30","committee":"Finance and Risk Committee of the Barbican Centre Board","time":"1.45 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-01","committee":"Freedom Applications Sub (Policy & Resources) Committee","time":"1.45 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-08","committee":"Court of Common Council","time":"1.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"City of London Police Pensions Board","time":"11.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-15","committee":"Health and Social Care Scrutiny Committee","time":"11.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-21","committee":"Committee of Aldermanic Almoners, Common Council Governors and Donation Governors of Christ's Hospital","time":"11.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Court of Common Council","time":"1.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"Audit and Risk Management Committee","time":"11.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Communications & Corporate Affairs Sub (Policy & Resources) Committee","time":"1.45 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Resource Allocation Sub (Policy and Resources) Committee","time":"1.45 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Finance Committee","time":"12.45 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"IT access management deficiencies: one user has diagnostic tool access, three can both develop and implement changes","lead":"Weak segregation of duties in the financial system increases the risk of unauthorized changes to the general ledger or supporting controls. This is a material control environment issue.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - City Fund ISA 260 Audit Findings Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk/documents/s236918/236918.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Control deficiency in journal approval \u2014 entries below \u00a3100,000 have no formal approval process","lead":"Absent formal approval controls on significant journal entries increases fraud and error risk. The finding that testing found no exceptions does not eliminate the underlying control gap.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - City Fund ISA 260 Audit Findings Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk/documents/s236918/236918.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"\u00a320.5m in accounting adjustments required, including \u00a350.87m overstatement of disposal gains","lead":"Material accounting errors requiring auditor correction indicate either accounting complexity, weak financial controls, or both. The scale of adjustments flags areas where lenders should expect close financial scrutiny.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - City Fund ISA 260 Audit Findings Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk/documents/s236918/236918.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Audit and Risk Management Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - City Fund ISA 260 Audit Findings Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk/documents/s236918/236918.pdf","headline":"IT access management deficiencies: one user has diagnostic tool access, three can both develop and implement changes","detail":"Auditors identified that one user had access to production environment diagnostic tools, and three users could both develop and implement system changes \u2014 a segregation of duties breach. Targeted testing of journals posted by affected users identified no exceptions, but the control weakness persists.","category":"audit","matters":"Weak segregation of duties in the financial system increases the risk of unauthorized changes to the general ledger or supporting controls. This is a material control environment issue.","figures":"1 user with diagnostic access to production; 3 users with dev and implementation access","quote":"Our IT audit identified control deficiencies relating to access management and segregation of duties. One user had access to diagnostic tools within the production environment, and three users had the ability to both develop and implement system changes.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Audit and Risk Management Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - City Fund ISA 260 Audit Findings Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk/documents/s236918/236918.pdf","headline":"Control deficiency in journal approval \u2014 entries below \u00a3100,000 have no formal approval process","detail":"The auditors identified that journal entries below \u00a3100,000 are not formally approved; only entries above that threshold receive formal review and approval. Targeted testing of unusual journal entries below the threshold identified no exceptions, but the control design remains deficient.","category":"audit","matters":"Absent formal approval controls on significant journal entries increases fraud and error risk. The finding that testing found no exceptions does not eliminate the underlying control gap.","figures":"\u00a3100,000 approval threshold","quote":"Consistent with prior years, we identified a control deficiency relating to the approval of journal entries. Journal lines below \u00a3100,000 are not subject to formal approval; with only retrospective review and approval performed for journal lines above this threshold","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Audit and Risk Management Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - City Fund ISA 260 Audit Findings Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk/documents/s236918/236918.pdf","headline":"\u00a320.5m in accounting adjustments required, including \u00a350.87m overstatement of disposal gains","detail":"Auditors identified adjustments totalling \u00a320.5m, including a material \u00a350.87m overstatement of gain on disposal (corrected to \u00a33.1m net), misclassification of \u00a36.236m of business rates as grant income, and \u00a33.421m overstatement of collection fund bad debt provision. All were corrected in the final accounts.","category":"audit","matters":"Material accounting errors requiring auditor correction indicate either accounting complexity, weak financial controls, or both. The scale of adjustments flags areas where lenders should expect close financial scrutiny.","figures":"\u00a320.5m total adjustment; gain on disposal overstated by \u00a350.87m; collection fund bad debt provision overstated \u00a33.421m","quote":"We identified adjustments to the financial statements and related disclosure notes, which resulted in a \u00a320.5m decrease in the Surplus on Provision of Services and on the level of the Authority's general fund.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Audit and Risk Management Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - City Fund ISA 260 Audit Findings Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk/documents/s236918/236918.pdf","headline":"Housing service regulator findings identified as new significant weakness in value for money arrangements","detail":"The auditors identified a new significant weakness in the current year relating to regulator findings from an inspection of the Corporation's housing service. The prior year significant weakness on the HRA reserve balance has been closed, but this new governance finding suggests operational or compliance issues in housing delivery.","category":"governance","matters":"Housing service regulatory failures affect operational risk and service delivery; for lenders monitoring local authority resilience, governance failures in a major service area are indicators of wider management issues.","figures":"New significant weakness identified; prior year HRA reserve weakness closed","quote":"However, we identified one new significant weakness in the current year in relation to Regulator findings following an inspection of the Corporation's housing service.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Audit and Risk Management Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 6 - City Fund Auditor&#39;s Annual Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk/documents/s236917/236917.pdf","headline":"HRA reserve remains critically low and is now planned on a one-year basis only, creating uncertainty beyond 2026-27.","detail":"The HRA reserve improved from a budgeted \u00a30.042m to actual \u00a30.205m in 2025-26, and is forecast to reach \u00a31.2m in 2026-27. However, this improvement depends on annual Exceptional Financial Support approval from government and the completion of housing income-generating projects. No forecasting exists beyond 2026-27.","category":"reserves","matters":"A lender needs visibility of HRA sustainability. One-year planning of a critical reserve introduces annual uncertainty. The reliance on discretionary government support (EFS) is contingent and not guaranteed beyond 2026-27.","figures":"HRA reserve \u00a30.205m at 31 March 2026 (budgeted \u00a30.042m); forecast to reach \u00a31.2m in 2026-27; \u00a32.65m EFS approved in principle for health and safety and repairs costs","quote":"The Authority forecasts its HRA on a one-year basis, and there is uncertainty as to the sustainability of its improved position beyond 2026-27.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-22"},"name":"City of London","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-23","since_iso":"2026-08-24","distress":true,"headline":"IT access management deficiencies: one user has diagnostic tool access, three can both develop and implement changes","lead":"Weak segregation of duties in the financial system increases the risk of unauthorized changes to the general ledger or supporting controls. This is a material control environment issue.","also":["16 other findings in this window","12 papers caught"],"watch":"Policy and Resources Committee on 2026-09-24","n_findings":17,"n_documents":12,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 2 - City Fund ISA 260 Audit Findings Report 2025-26","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk/documents/s236918/236918.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":101,"news_drafts_total":3}}